{"title": "Australia’s electric ferry trials: How a lack of foresight drives weak ambition", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australias-electric-ferry-trials-how-a-lack-of-foresight-drives-weak-ambition/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australias-electric-ferry-trials-how-a-lack-of-foresight-drives-weak-ambition/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Australia’s electric ferry trials: How a lack of foresight drives weak ambition\"><img alt=\"Incat 130m electric ferry\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2023/01/Incat_02_small-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Electric ferries have gone from novelty to common sense in less than a decade. But Australian governments are still pretending the technology is still at the starting line?</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australias-electric-ferry-trials-how-a-lack-of-foresight-drives-weak-ambition/\">Australia’s electric ferry trials: How a lack of foresight drives weak ambition</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-19T22:27:43+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-20T08:21:12.565108+00:00"}
{"title": "Germany launches new electric car subsidy aimed at low-income households", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/germany-launches-new-electric-car-subsidy-aimed-at-low-income-households/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/germany-launches-new-electric-car-subsidy-aimed-at-low-income-households/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Germany launches new electric car subsidy aimed at low-income households\"><img alt=\"EV sales\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2024/10/20220427001652035168-original-380x285.jpeg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Germany launches new subsidy program for electric vehicles, offering up to €6,000 to lower-income households buying or leasing new EVs.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/germany-launches-new-electric-car-subsidy-aimed-at-low-income-households/\">Germany launches new electric car subsidy aimed at low-income households</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-19T21:06:15+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-20T08:21:12.565108+00:00"}
{"title": "Australian start-up crunches the numbers on electric trucks for companies stuck on diesel", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australian-start-up-crunches-the-numbers-on-electric-trucks-for-companies-stuck-on-diesel/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australian-start-up-crunches-the-numbers-on-electric-trucks-for-companies-stuck-on-diesel/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Australian start-up crunches the numbers on electric trucks for companies stuck on diesel\"><img alt=\"volvo trucks linfox\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/05/volvo-linfox-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>How far and how fast can a battery-powered prime mover go? One Australian start-up is doing the sums so freight businesses looking to move from diesel don't have to.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/australian-start-up-crunches-the-numbers-on-electric-trucks-for-companies-stuck-on-diesel/\">Australian start-up crunches the numbers on electric trucks for companies stuck on diesel</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-19T20:35:31+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-20T08:21:12.565108+00:00"}
{"title": "BYD sends its own ship with almost 5,000 NEVs to meet surging demand in Australia market", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/byd-sends-its-own-ship-with-almost-5000-nevs-to-meet-surging-demand-in-australia-market/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/byd-sends-its-own-ship-with-almost-5000-nevs-to-meet-surging-demand-in-australia-market/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"BYD sends its own ship with almost 5,000 NEVs to meet surging demand in Australia market\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/7012160-82a9ca8b-1c35-deb5-9076-8764c93296d1-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>In a first for the Australian EV market, Chinese car giant BYD has dispatched its own ship with thousands of NEVs to meet the surge in local demand.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/20/byd-sends-its-own-ship-with-almost-5000-nevs-to-meet-surging-demand-in-australia-market/\">BYD sends its own ship with almost 5,000 NEVs to meet surging demand in Australia market</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-19T14:47:08+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-20T08:21:12.565108+00:00"}
{"title": "Construction starts on Sydney’s first purpose-built electric bus depot", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/construction-starts-on-sydneys-first-purpose-built-electric-bus-depot/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/construction-starts-on-sydneys-first-purpose-built-electric-bus-depot/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Construction starts on Sydney’s first purpose-built electric bus depot\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2025/10/ZEB-251002-Macquarie-Park-Depot-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Construction has officially begun on Sydney’s first purpose-built electric bus depot, which will be capable of charging 150 battery electric buses.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/construction-starts-on-sydneys-first-purpose-built-electric-bus-depot/\">Construction starts on Sydney’s first purpose-built electric bus depot</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-19T00:23:02+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-20T08:21:12.565108+00:00"}
{"title": "Sydney Harbour expected to have its first electric ferry within two years", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/sydney-harbour-expected-to-have-its-first-electric-ferry-within-two-years/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/sydney-harbour-expected-to-have-its-first-electric-ferry-within-two-years/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Sydney Harbour expected to have its first electric ferry within two years\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Parramatta-River-Class-ferry-Transport-for-NSW-FB-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>Sydney Harbour is expected to have its first electric ferry within two years - beginning a trial that will decide whether more electric ferries will join the fleet. </p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/sydney-harbour-expected-to-have-its-first-electric-ferry-within-two-years/\">Sydney Harbour expected to have its first electric ferry within two years</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-19T00:19:26+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-20T08:21:12.565108+00:00"}
{"title": "Video: Hyundai Elexio review – Fighting China with China?", "link": "https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/video-hyundai-elexio-review-fighting-china-with-china/", "summary": "<a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/video-hyundai-elexio-review-fighting-china-with-china/\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"Video: Hyundai Elexio review – Fighting China with China?\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image\" height=\"285\" src=\"https://thedriven.io/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/YouTube-Thumbnails-1920-x-1080-px-25-380x285.jpg\" style=\"display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear: both;\" width=\"380\" /></a><p>In this review, we look at how the Hyundai Elexio stacks up against rivals like Tesla and BYD - and whether it does enough to stand out.</p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://thedriven.io/2026/05/19/video-hyundai-elexio-review-fighting-china-with-china/\">Video: Hyundai Elexio review – Fighting China with China?</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://thedriven.io\">The Driven</a>.</p>", "published": "2026-05-18T21:44:28+00:00", "source": "The Driven", "category": "mobility", "matched_entities": {}, "logged_at": "2026-05-20T08:21:12.565108+00:00"}
